  "monitoring": [
    "FBC, U&Es (including electrolytes), LFTs (including albumin) before each cycle",
    "Nadir ANC and nadir platelets must be documented after each cycle — required for DA-EPOCH dose adjustment next cycle",
    "Regular blood glucose monitoring (prednisolone-related hyperglycaemia risk)",
    "G-CSF (filgrastim) mandatory from day 6 until ANC ≥1.0×10⁹/L post-nadir",
    "LVEF monitoring at baseline and as clinically indicated (cumulative doxorubicin toxicity)",
    "Rituximab infusion vital signs monitoring (temperature, BP, pulse, O2 sats) during every infusion",
    "Central line assessment and care throughout continuous infusion (days 1-4)",
    "Hepatitis B monitoring if positive serology detected — expert review required",
    "Neurological assessment before each cycle (vincristine neuropathy monitoring)"
  ],
  "warnings": [
    "CENTRAL LINE MANDATORY for this protocol. Etoposide, doxorubicin and vincristine must be administered via central venous catheter — peripheral administration is contraindicated.",
    "G-CSF (filgrastim/lenograstim) is MANDATORY from Day 6 of every cycle. Record nadir ANC and nadir platelets — required for dose adjustment next cycle.",
    "DOSE ADJUSTMENT after every cycle based on nadir counts: escalate by 20% if nadir ANC ≥0.5 AND platelets ≥25; reduce by 20% if ANC <0.5 on >2 days OR platelets <25 on >2 days.",
    "Check hepatitis B status before starting rituximab — risk of fatal reactivation.",
    "PCP prophylaxis (co-trimoxazole) is MANDATORY throughout treatment and for 6 months after.",
    "Risk of progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy (PML) with rituximab.",
    "Maximum lifetime cumulative doxorubicin dose: 450 mg/m² (400 mg/m² if prior mediastinal/pericardial radiotherapy).",
    "Vincristine in this protocol has NO routine dose cap — doses based on actual body weight. ARIA automatically caps at 2.4m² and may need manual adjustment.",
    "Cytokine release syndrome risk with rituximab — medicinal products for allergic reactions must be immediately available.",
    "Prednisolone is a FLAT 100mg dose (NOT BSA-dosed) — patient self-administers on morning of treatment and Days 2-5 at home.",
    "COMBINATION BAG: doxorubicin, etoposide and vincristine are mixed in the SAME 1000ml NaCl 0.9% bag. Each bag administered over 48 hours on Day 1 and Day 3. On ARIA only doxorubicin will have a volume/rate — this is by design.",
    "Dose adjustments from cycle 2 apply to cyclophosphamide, doxorubicin and etoposide only (not vincristine). Monitored by FBC on days 9, 12, 15 and 18.",
    "Allopurinol 300mg once daily for 7 days (cycle 1 only).",
    "Cyclophosphamide: consider mesna in patients with pre-existing bladder disorders (oral 40% of cyclophosphamide dose at 0, 2, 6 hours).",
    "Where significant reductions in albumin levels occur, consider reducing the dose of etoposide.",
    "DOSE ESCALATION BELOW LEVEL 1: Where doses have been previously reduced below level 1, any subsequent dose escalations apply to cyclophosphamide ONLY — do NOT escalate doxorubicin or etoposide."
  ],
